  "notes": "A mesh of identical cores: core (i, j) keeps row i of A in its own local memory and one accumulator, and multiplies and accumulates when a valid message arrives on its only input link, from the north; each core's router passes the message one core south per cycle. The edge feeds column 0 of B into the mesh from the start edge and column j j cycles later, so the cores of one row stay apart in time; the far core raises done. Latency 3N - 2 (10 at N = 4). The local memories have N*N*N*W bits, more than 2^31 at some in-range points.",
  "player": "gridwren",
